Out of sample, Nov 2001 to Oct 2026
───────────────────────────────────
  Method            Return  Volatility  Sharpe  Drawdown  CVaR 95%  Turnover
  Equal weight        7.7%       11.4%    0.55    −37.8%      6.9%       10%
  Minimum variance    5.8%        8.4%    0.50    −22.3%      4.7%       15%
  Maximum Sharpe      6.1%       10.6%    0.44    −40.8%      6.6%       35%

  Return, volatility and turnover a year, turnover one-way (the share of value
  bought, or sold); drawdown the largest fall; CVaR the average loss in the
  worst 5% of periods. Equal weight: fully invested and long only; the limits on
  weights do not apply. Maximum Sharpe found no weights at 6 refits, from Jun
  2008 to Sep 2009 (infeasible); it kept the weights it held.

In sample and out of sample
───────────────────────────
  Method            Sharpe in  Sharpe out  Change  Return in  Return out
  Equal weight           0.55        0.55    0.00       7.7%        7.7%
  Minimum variance       0.59        0.50   −0.09       6.5%        5.8%
  Maximum Sharpe         0.64        0.44   −0.20       7.1%        6.1%
  In sample, each method is fitted to the whole history and scored on the
  periods tested, Nov 2001 to Oct 2026: it sees the returns it is scored on, so
  it looks better than it can be. The gap to out of sample is the cost of
  estimating from the past.

